-/* ==========================================================================
-   KiwiCaptcha widget — Mono Checksum design language (2026-09-05)
-   ============================================================================
-   The unified platform language: four motifs, zero ornament.
+/* KiwiCaptcha — Spiral Lock interface.
+   Passive security status, one progress track, one native recovery control.
+   All selectors are widget-scoped; tokens remain integrator-overridable.
+   The logo is static. Motion, when present, is a progress-width transition. */
 
-   - SLOT: the flip-cell. The badge and the seven-cell checksum strip are
-     slots; states recolor them. Motion: settle 250ms, stagger 120ms —
-     never a loop faster than the eye can dismiss.
-   - NEEDLE: one solid among faint (the winning nonce). The icon chip in
-     its faint state is the search space; done is the found proof.
-   - RECEIPT: mono rows (challenge · work · proof) — the info line's
-     typography, ready for pipeline detail.
-   - HAIRLINE: the 2px progress track. No gradients, no glow, no shine
-     sweep, no scale bounce. State changes are color + width, 200ms.
-
-   A11y contract preserved from the prior skin: sr-only live region,
-     >=44px retry target, 2px focus ring at >=3:1, red never used for
-     text (icon/chip only), badge text >=11px, prefers-reduced-motion
-     kills every decorative animation.
-   ========================================================================== */
